      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the visual representation of the 'foreigner'",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man wearing a kufi, who is used to represent the 'foreigner' in the meme's context. The meme implies that the user (as a gay guy) is the recipient of messages from foreigners, and the visual of the man is used to symbolize the 'foreigner' who is supposedly 'stoned' (unwelcome) to gay men. This creates a projection where the user identifies with the gay guy in the text, and the man in the image is the projected entity representing the 'foreigner' who is the subject of the stereotype.",
